# G1 (from tp4-gluefix-jobs G1, retargeted): the EXACT audited smoke of the GDN odd-user pair slice on c2-packed-tp4-gate-pairslice (the V2 glue OFF, so QWEN_FAST_GDN_PAIR_SLICE=1 is the live path,
# with the audits on). Note: the best-ship-glue and best-gate-glue profiles keep V2 on, which replaces the slices the flag shortens, so they only prove the flag is harmless beside V2; this is
# the arm that can show the slice engaged.
# READ: the pair-slice engaged marker in the log, c2_smoke_check clean, every audit mismatches=0, texts and concurrent4_code_equal hashes equal to the same-image control (c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace
# texts of the gluefix window), concurrent4_code_32k complete. Duration (estimate): 60 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-pairslice
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent4_code_32k
